From 1eea0c78e0e77874a077b05f7cb55922fa15c972 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:57:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-10: snaplines, multi-select, align / make same
 size -- WPF designer operations (0.10.0)

- snaplines: while dragging or resizing, the moving edges / centres snap (5px)
  to the edges and centres of the siblings in the same container and of the
  container; a red guide is drawn; Alt = no snapping
- multi-select like WPF: Ctrl+click / Shift+click add or remove, the last one
  clicked is primary; pressing a member drags the whole selection, a click
  without moving keeps only that one; arrows / Ctrl+arrows move / resize the
  whole selection
- align & size (WPF Format > Align): left / h-centre / right / top / v-centre /
  bottom / same width / height / size, relative to the primary; buttons in the
  properties panel when several are selected
- a group move or an alignment is ONE message -> ONE WorkspaceEdit -> ONE undo
  step (unchanged tags are not written; overlapping edits are refused)
- "operate once" moved off Ctrl+click (now multi-select) to the operate-mode
  toggle; tabs still switch in design mode

Tests: probe 2 pages x 20 asserted (multi-select, group drag = one batch,
align top, snap, operate mode) / fake vscode 53 (batch = one WorkspaceEdit,
unchanged skipped) / real VS Code 52: multi-select + same height -> ONE undo
restores the page exactly; never saved, opened files byte-identical (MD5).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
